  "description": "It was discovered that OpenVPN had a use-after-free vulnerability in\nits TLS session handling. An attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause OpenVPN to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or\nexecute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-84471)\n\nIt was discovered that OpenVPN incorrectly handled retransmissions of\nACK packet IDs, which could trigger a timeout integer overflow. A\nremote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of\nservice. (CVE-2026-84732)",
  "id": "USN-8852-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in OpenVPN.",
